#!perl

# PODNAME: git-tms
# ABSTRACT: Read, push and fetch the test results that git notes keep

use 5.014;

use strict;
use warnings FATAL => 'all';

use Git::TMS::CLI ();

exit Git::TMS::CLI::main(@ARGV);

__END__

=head1 SYNOPSIS

    git tms results [--config NAME]... [--raw] [REVISION | RANGE]
    git tms scan --where-fails TEST [REVISION]
    git tms push [REMOTE]
    git tms fetch [REMOTE]
    git tms help

=head1 DESCRIPTION

The harness plugins of L<Git::TMS> write the outcome of each test file to the
notes of the tested tree, one notes ref for each configuration.  This program
reads those notes, and moves them between repositories.  Git runs it for
C<git tms>, because it is called F<git-tms> and is on the C<PATH>.

C<git tms help> prints each command and what it does.  L<Git::TMS::CLI> has
the same text.

=head1 SEE ALSO

L<Git::TMS>

L<Git::TMS::CLI>

=cut
